          "date": "2026-11-25 16:18:57.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21328 efalnd: Undo a partial Tx mapping on failure",
        "message": "LU-21328 efalnd: Undo a partial Tx mapping on failure\n\nWhen DMA mapping a Tx failed, its fragment count was left set, so\nreleasing the Tx later tried to unmap fragments that were never\nmapped.\n\nHave the mapping clean up after itself on any failure and clear the\nfragment count, so a failed mapping leaves nothing for the Tx release\nto undo.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 0c773016d837 (\"LU-18977 efalnd: Introduce AWS EFA Lustre network driver\")\nChange-Id: Id23324b5a522475ccfa778e4dbf5f73718c805d1\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
